      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> Wire mesh MOQs from Chinese factories are lower than most buyers expect — standard rolls often start at 1–5 rolls (a few hundred dollars), while custom specs typically run 100–500 m or 1–3 tons. The three rules that protect you: (1) always pay for samples from your top 2–3 factories — paid samples signal a real buyer, get production-line (not warehouse-shelf) material, and arrive faster than "free" ones; (2) compare samples from all three factories against one written spec sheet with a micrometer, scale, and coating gauge before approving any; (3) place a trial order of roughly 20% of your expected annual volume, sized to fill a workable shipping unit, and treat it as a paid audition for the factory. This guide gives you the MOQ norms per product type, the sampling playbook, and the trial-order framework.
      </p>
    </div>

