      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Minimum order quantity is where more wire mesh deals stall than anywhere else. Buyers assume factories want container loads; factories assume small buyers will disappear after one order. Both assumptions are wrong often enough to be expensive. In Anping's hyper-competitive market, MOQs are negotiable, sampling is cheap insurance, and the trial order is the standard way serious relationships begin. If you are new to importing, read the <a href="/sourcing-guide/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">sourcing guide</a> and the <a href="/blog/how-to-import-wire-mesh-from-china/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">import step-by-step guide</a> first; this article covers the three decision points where buyers most often lose money.
      </p>
